Chapter: Risk
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter Random

 We say:

Section: The Rules

 The rules as Hasbro publishes them (Risk, the classic game's rules
 leaflet), for two to four players.

 Rule 1. The board is 42 territories in six continents: North America (9
 territories, 5 bonus armies), South America (4, 2), Europe (7, 5), Africa
 (6, 3), Asia (12, 7) and Australia (4, 2). Territories are adjacent where
 they share a border or a sea line.

 Rule 2. Setting up: the territories are dealt round the table, one army on
 each, and the players then place the rest of their starting armies one at
 a time in turn, each on a territory of their own. Two players start with
 40 armies, three with 35, four with 30.

 Rule 3. A turn is three parts in order: reinforce, attack, fortify.

 Rule 4. Reinforcing: the player receives the territories they hold divided
 by three, at least 3, plus each continent's bonus for a continent they
 hold whole, plus armies for any set of cards traded in, and places them
 on their own territories.

 Rule 5. Cards: 42 territory cards, each showing an infantry, a cavalry or
 an artillery, and 2 wild cards. A set is three cards of one symbol, one of
 each, or any two with a wild card. A set trades in during reinforcement
 for 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 15 armies, and 5 more for each set after, counted
 over every player's trades. A traded card showing a territory the player
 holds puts 2 more armies on it, at most once a turn. A player holding five
 or more cards at the start of their turn must trade.

 Rule 6. Attacking: from a territory of theirs with at least two armies,
 the player attacks an adjacent enemy territory, rolling 1, 2 or 3 dice as
 they choose, at most one fewer than the armies there. The defender rolls
 1 or 2 dice, at most the armies defending. The highest dice are compared
 in pairs; the higher die wins each pair and a tie goes to the defender,
 each lost pair costing one army. A player may attack any number of times.

 Rule 7. A territory emptied of defenders is conquered: the attacker moves
 in at least as many armies as dice rolled in that battle, and at most all
 but one of the attacking territory's armies.

 Rule 8. A player who conquers at least one territory in a turn draws one
 card at the end of it. A player who eliminates another takes their cards,
 and holding six or more then trades in sets at once until they hold four
 or fewer, placing those armies before attacking on.

 Rule 9. Fortifying: the turn ends with at most one move of armies from one
 territory to another of the player's own connected to it through their own
 territories, leaving at least one army behind.

 Rule 10. The player who holds all 42 territories wins.

 Where the rules leave a choice, this engine takes these. The defender
 always rolls as many dice as allowed. The deal and the deck are shuffled
 from the game's seed, the first player to set up plays first, and two
 players play without the neutral army. A card's symbol is its territory
 number modulo 3 (infantry, cavalry, artillery), 14 of each as the deck
 has. Traded cards go to a discard pile that is shuffled into a new deck
 when the deck runs out. The 2 armies for a held territory go to the first
 such card of the set in territory order. A game nobody has won after 400
 turns has no winner.

Section: Types

  RiskState = record {
    cells : List Integer
  }

  RiskResult = record {
    winner      : Integer,
    turns       : Integer,
    territories : List Integer
  }

Section: The State Layout

 The state is one Integer list of 280 slots. Slots 0 to 31 are the fields
 named below, with the starting armies each player has left to place at 26
 to 29. Territories sit at 40 in strides of 2 (owner, armies). Each card's
 holder sits at 130 (-2 the deck, -1 the discard pile, else a player); the
 deck's order at 180 and the discard pile's at 230, each 44 slots.

  rk-f-np : Integer
  rk-f-np = 0

  rk-f-cur : Integer
  rk-f-cur = 1

  rk-f-turn : Integer
  rk-f-turn = 2

  rk-f-over : Integer
  rk-f-over = 3

  rk-f-winner : Integer
  rk-f-winner = 4

  rk-f-phase : Integer
  rk-f-phase = 5

  rk-f-place : Integer
  rk-f-place = 6

  rk-f-trades : Integer
  rk-f-trades = 7

  rk-f-conquered : Integer
  rk-f-conquered = 8

  rk-f-bonus : Integer
  rk-f-bonus = 9

  rk-f-mfrom : Integer
  rk-f-mfrom = 10

  rk-f-mto : Integer
  rk-f-mto = 11

  rk-f-mmin : Integer
  rk-f-mmin = 12

  rk-f-human : Integer
  rk-f-human = 13

  rk-f-seed : Integer
  rk-f-seed = 14

  rk-f-reshuffles : Integer
  rk-f-reshuffles = 15

  rk-f-dice : Integer
  rk-f-dice = 16

  rk-f-alost : Integer
  rk-f-alost = 21

  rk-f-dlost : Integer
  rk-f-dlost = 22

  rk-f-decklen : Integer
  rk-f-decklen = 23

  rk-f-discardlen : Integer
  rk-f-discardlen = 24

  rk-f-setup : Integer
  rk-f-setup = 26

  rk-f-rolled : Integer
  rk-f-rolled = 30

  rk-f-elim : Integer
  rk-f-elim = 31

  rk-size : Integer
  rk-size = 280

  rk-tslot : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-tslot (t) (f) = 40 + t * 2 + f

 Phases: 0 setting up, 1 reinforcing, 2 attacking, 3 moving in after a
 conquest, 4 fortifying, 5 trading and placing after an elimination, 6
 over.

 Actions: 0 place an army, 1 trade a set (three card numbers packed as
 a + 64 b + 4096 c), 2 attack (from, to and dice packed the same way), 3
 stop attacking, 4 move in, 5 fortify (from, to and armies packed), 6 end
 the turn without fortifying.

Section: Reading And Writing

  rk-get : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-get (s) (i) = list-at (s.cells) i

  rk-put : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-put (s) (i) (v) =
    let c = list-set-at (s.cells) i v
    in s

  rk-copy : RiskState -> RiskState
  rk-copy (s) = RiskState { cells = rk-copy-cells (s.cells) 0 (list-length (s.cells)) [] }

  rk-copy-cells : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  rk-copy-cells (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else rk-copy-cells xs (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  rk-players : RiskState -> Integer
  rk-players (s) = rk-get s rk-f-np

  rk-cur : RiskState -> Integer
  rk-cur (s) = rk-get s rk-f-cur

  rk-phase : RiskState -> Integer
  rk-phase (s) = rk-get s rk-f-phase

  rk-over : RiskState -> Boolean
  rk-over (s) = rk-get s rk-f-over == 1

  rk-owner : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-owner (s) (t) = rk-get s (rk-tslot t 0)

  rk-armies : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-armies (s) (t) = rk-get s (rk-tslot t 1)

  rk-set-armies : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-set-armies (s) (t) (n) = rk-put s (rk-tslot t 1) n

  rk-holder : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-holder (s) (c) = rk-get s (130 + c)

  rk-unpack-a : Integer -> Integer
  rk-unpack-a (x) = rng-mod x 64

  rk-unpack-b : Integer -> Integer
  rk-unpack-b (x) = rng-mod (x / 64) 64

  rk-unpack-c : Integer -> Integer
  rk-unpack-c (x) = x / 4096

  rk-pack : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-pack (a) (b) (c) = a + 64 * b + 4096 * c

Section: The Board

 Territories: North America 0 Alaska, 1 Northwest Territory, 2 Greenland,
 3 Alberta, 4 Ontario, 5 Quebec, 6 Western United States, 7 Eastern United
 States, 8 Central America; South America 9 Venezuela, 10 Peru, 11 Brazil,
 12 Argentina; Europe 13 Iceland, 14 Scandinavia, 15 Great Britain, 16
 Northern Europe, 17 Ukraine, 18 Western Europe, 19 Southern Europe; Africa
 20 North Africa, 21 Egypt, 22 East Africa, 23 Congo, 24 South Africa, 25
 Madagascar; Asia 26 Ural, 27 Siberia, 28 Yakutsk, 29 Kamchatka, 30
 Irkutsk, 31 Mongolia, 32 Japan, 33 Afghanistan, 34 China, 35 Middle East,
 36 India, 37 Siam; Australia 38 Indonesia, 39 New Guinea, 40 Western
 Australia, 41 Eastern Australia.

  rk-territories : Integer
  rk-territories = 42

  rk-continent : Integer -> Integer
  rk-continent (t) =
    if t <= 8 then 0
    else if t <= 12 then 1
    else if t <= 19 then 2
    else if t <= 25 then 3
    else if t <= 37 then 4
    else 5

  rk-continent-bonus : Integer -> Integer
  rk-continent-bonus (c) =
    if c == 0 then 5
    else if c == 1 then 2
    else if c == 2 then 5
    else if c == 3 then 3
    else if c == 4 then 7
    else 2

 Each border once, from the lower-numbered territory: 83 borders.

  rk-border : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-border (a) (b) =
    if a == 0 then b == 1 | b == 3 | b == 29
    else if a == 1 then b == 2 | b == 3 | b == 4
    else if a == 2 then b == 4 | b == 5 | b == 13
    else if a == 3 then b == 4 | b == 6
    else if a == 4 then b == 5 | b == 6 | b == 7
    else if a == 5 then b == 7
    else if a == 6 then b == 7 | b == 8
    else if a == 7 then b == 8
    else if a == 8 then b == 9
    else if a == 9 then b == 10 | b == 11
    else if a == 10 then b == 11 | b == 12
    else if a == 11 then b == 12 | b == 20
    else if a == 13 then b == 14 | b == 15
    else if a == 14 then b == 15 | b == 16 | b == 17
    else if a == 15 then b == 16 | b == 18
    else if a == 16 then b == 17 | b == 18 | b == 19
    else if a == 17 then b == 19 | b == 26 | b == 33 | b == 35
    else if a == 18 then b == 19 | b == 20
    else if a == 19 then b == 20 | b == 21 | b == 35
    else if a == 20 then b == 21 | b == 22 | b == 23
    else if a == 21 then b == 22 | b == 35
    else if a == 22 then b == 23 | b == 24 | b == 25 | b == 35
    else if a == 23 then b == 24
    else if a == 24 then b == 25
    else if a == 26 then b == 27 | b == 33 | b == 34
    else if a == 27 then b == 28 | b == 30 | b == 31 | b == 34
    else if a == 28 then b == 29 | b == 30
    else if a == 29 then b == 30 | b == 31 | b == 32
    else if a == 30 then b == 31
    else if a == 31 then b == 32 | b == 34
    else if a == 33 then b == 34 | b == 35 | b == 36
    else if a == 34 then b == 36 | b == 37
    else if a == 35 then b == 36
    else if a == 36 then b == 37
    else if a == 37 then b == 38
    else if a == 38 then b == 39 | b == 40
    else if a == 39 then b == 40 | b == 41
    else if a == 40 then b == 41
    else False

  rk-adjacent : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-adjacent (a) (b) =
    if a < 0 | b < 0 | a >= rk-territories | b >= rk-territories then False
    else if a < b then rk-border a b
    else if b < a then rk-border b a
    else False

Section: Dice

 The Rng's low bit alternates from one state to the next, so dice drawn
 from consecutive states are correlated; each die folds the high bits of
 its own mix down instead.

  rk-die : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-die (seed) (k) = 1 + rng-mod (bit-shru (mix-bits seed k) 1) 6

  rk-rand : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-rand (seed) (k) (n) = rng-mod (bit-shru (mix-bits seed k) 1) n

Section: Counting

  rk-held : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-held (s) (p) = rk-held-loop s p 0 0

  rk-held-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-held-loop (s) (p) (t) (acc) =
    if t >= rk-territories then acc
    else rk-held-loop s p (t + 1) (acc + (if rk-owner s t == p then 1 else 0))

  rk-total-armies : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-total-armies (s) (p) = rk-total-loop s p 0 0

  rk-total-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-total-loop (s) (p) (t) (acc) =
    if t >= rk-territories then acc
    else rk-total-loop s p (t + 1) (acc + (if rk-owner s t == p then rk-armies s t else 0))

  rk-holds-continent : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-holds-continent (s) (p) (c) = rk-holds-cont-loop s p c 0

  rk-holds-cont-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-holds-cont-loop (s) (p) (c) (t) =
    if t >= rk-territories then True
    else if rk-continent t /= c then rk-holds-cont-loop s p c (t + 1)
    else if rk-owner s t /= p then False
    else rk-holds-cont-loop s p c (t + 1)

  rk-bonus-total : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-bonus-total (s) (p) (c) (acc) =
    if c >= 6 then acc
    else rk-bonus-total s p (c + 1) (acc + (if rk-holds-continent s p c then rk-continent-bonus c else 0))

  rk-reinforcements : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-reinforcements (s) (p) =
    let base = rk-held s p / 3
    in (if base < 3 then 3 else base) + rk-bonus-total s p 0 0

  rk-alive : RiskState, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-alive (s) (p) = rk-held s p > 0

  rk-hand : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-hand (s) (p) = rk-hand-loop s p 0 0

  rk-hand-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-hand-loop (s) (p) (c) (acc) =
    if c >= 44 then acc
    else rk-hand-loop s p (c + 1) (acc + (if rk-holder s c == p then 1 else 0))

Section: Setting Up

  rk-zeros : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  rk-zeros (n) (acc) =
    if n <= 0 then acc
    else rk-zeros (n - 1) (list-push acc 0)

  rk-start-armies : Integer -> Integer
  rk-start-armies (np) = if np <= 2 then 40 else if np == 3 then 35 else 30

  risk-init : Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  risk-init (seed) (num-players) =
    let np = if num-players < 2 then 2 else if num-players > 4 then 4 else num-players
    in let s0 = RiskState { cells = rk-zeros rk-size [] }
    in let s1 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s0 rk-f-np np) rk-f-winner (-1)) rk-f-human (-1)) rk-f-seed seed
    in let s2 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s1 rk-f-mfrom (-1)) rk-f-mto (-1)) rk-f-decklen 44
    in let s3 = rk-deal-assign (rk-deal-shuffle (rk-order-fill s2 0) seed 41) np 0
    in let s4 = rk-setup-left s3 0 np
    in let s5 = rk-deck-fill s4 0
    in rk-deck-shuffle s5 seed 43

 The deal's order is shuffled in the discard slots, which are empty until
 the first trade, and then dealt round the table.

  rk-order-fill : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-order-fill (s) (i) =
    if i >= rk-territories then s
    else rk-order-fill (rk-put s (230 + i) i) (i + 1)

  rk-deal-shuffle : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-deal-shuffle (s) (seed) (i) =
    if i <= 0 then s
    else let j = rk-rand seed (1000 + i) (i + 1)
    in let a = rk-get s (230 + i)
    in let b = rk-get s (230 + j)
    in rk-deal-shuffle (rk-put (rk-put s (230 + i) b) (230 + j) a) seed (i - 1)

  rk-deal-assign : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-deal-assign (s) (np) (i) =
    if i >= rk-territories then s
    else let t = rk-get s (230 + i)
    in rk-deal-assign (rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s (rk-tslot t 0) (rng-mod i np)) (rk-tslot t 1) 1) (230 + i) 0) np (i + 1)

  rk-setup-left : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-setup-left (s) (p) (np) =
    if p >= np then s
    else rk-setup-left (rk-put s (rk-f-setup + p) (rk-start-armies np - rk-held s p)) (p + 1) np

  rk-deck-fill : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-deck-fill (s) (c) =
    if c >= 44 then s
    else rk-deck-fill (rk-put (rk-put s (180 + c) c) (130 + c) (-2)) (c + 1)

  rk-deck-shuffle : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-deck-shuffle (s) (seed) (i) =
    if i <= 0 then s
    else let j = rk-rand seed (3000 + i) (i + 1)
    in let a = rk-get s (180 + i)
    in let b = rk-get s (180 + j)
    in rk-deck-shuffle (rk-put (rk-put s (180 + i) b) (180 + j) a) seed (i - 1)

  rk-set-human : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-set-human (s) (p) = rk-put s rk-f-human p

Section: Cards

  rk-symbol : Integer -> Integer
  rk-symbol (c) = if c >= 42 then 3 else rng-mod c 3

  rk-set-ok : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-set-ok (a) (b) (c) =
    let x = rk-symbol a
    in let y = rk-symbol b
    in let z = rk-symbol c
    in if x == 3 | y == 3 | z == 3 then True
    else if x == y & y == z then True
    else x /= y & y /= z & x /= z

  rk-trade-value : Integer -> Integer
  rk-trade-value (k) =
    if k == 0 then 4
    else if k == 1 then 6
    else if k == 2 then 8
    else if k == 3 then 10
    else if k == 4 then 12
    else 15 + 5 * (k - 5)

  rk-can-trade-cards : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-can-trade-cards (s) (p) (packed) =
    let a = rk-unpack-a packed
    in let b = rk-unpack-b packed
    in let c = rk-unpack-c packed
    in if a >= b | b >= c | c >= 44 | a < 0 then False
    else if rk-holder s a /= p | rk-holder s b /= p | rk-holder s c /= p then False
    else rk-set-ok a b c

  rk-discard : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-discard (s) (c) =
    let n = rk-get s rk-f-discardlen
    in rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s (230 + n) c) rk-f-discardlen (n + 1)) (130 + c) (-1)

  rk-trade : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-trade (s) (p) (packed) =
    let a = rk-unpack-a packed
    in let b = rk-unpack-b packed
    in let c = rk-unpack-c packed
    in let k = rk-get s rk-f-trades
    in let s2 = rk-put (rk-put s rk-f-trades (k + 1)) rk-f-place (rk-get s rk-f-place + rk-trade-value k)
    in let s3 = rk-discard (rk-discard (rk-discard s2 a) b) c
    in if rk-get s3 rk-f-bonus == 1 then s3
    else rk-trade-bonus s3 p (rk-bonus-card s3 p a b c)

  rk-bonus-card : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-bonus-card (s) (p) (a) (b) (c) =
    if a < 42 & rk-owner s a == p then a
    else if b < 42 & rk-owner s b == p then b
    else if c < 42 & rk-owner s c == p then c
    else (-1)

  rk-trade-bonus : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-trade-bonus (s) (p) (t) =
    if t < 0 then s
    else rk-put (rk-set-armies s t (rk-armies s t + 2)) rk-f-bonus 1

 A card is drawn from the top; an empty deck is first remade from the
 discard pile, shuffled.

  rk-draw : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-draw (s) (p) =
    let s2 = if rk-get s rk-f-decklen == 0 then rk-reshuffle s else s
    in let n = rk-get s2 rk-f-decklen
    in if n == 0 then s2
    else let c = rk-get s2 180
    in rk-put (rk-put (rk-deck-shift s2 0 n) rk-f-decklen (n - 1)) (130 + c) p

  rk-deck-shift : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-deck-shift (s) (k) (n) =
    if k + 1 >= n then s
    else rk-deck-shift (rk-put s (180 + k) (rk-get s (181 + k))) (k + 1) n

  rk-reshuffle : RiskState -> RiskState
  rk-reshuffle (s) =
    let n = rk-get s rk-f-discardlen
    in let r = rk-get s rk-f-reshuffles
    in let s2 = rk-move-discards s 0 n
    in let s3 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s2 rk-f-decklen n) rk-f-discardlen 0) rk-f-reshuffles (r + 1)
    in rk-deck-shuffle-from s3 (rk-get s rk-f-seed) (5000 + r * 64) (n - 1)

  rk-move-discards : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-move-discards (s) (k) (n) =
    if k >= n then s
    else let c = rk-get s (230 + k)
    in rk-move-discards (rk-put (rk-put s (180 + k) c) (130 + c) (-2)) (k + 1) n

  rk-deck-shuffle-from : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-deck-shuffle-from (s) (seed) (base) (i) =
    if i <= 0 then s
    else let j = rk-rand seed (base + i) (i + 1)
    in let a = rk-get s (180 + i)
    in let b = rk-get s (180 + j)
    in rk-deck-shuffle-from (rk-put (rk-put s (180 + i) b) (180 + j) a) seed base (i - 1)

  rk-take-cards : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-take-cards (s) (from) (to) (c) =
    if c >= 44 then s
    else rk-take-cards (if rk-holder s c == from then rk-put s (130 + c) to else s) from to (c + 1)

Section: Connection

 Whether two territories of a player are joined through that player's own
 territories: a flood from `a` over a 42-bit mask of reached territories,
 expanding each reached territory once.

  rk-connected : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-connected (s) (p) (a) (b) = rk-has (rk-flood s p (rk-bit a) 0) b

  rk-bit : Integer -> Integer
  rk-bit (t) = if t <= 0 then 1 else 2 * rk-bit (t - 1)

  rk-has : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-has (mask) (t) = rng-mod (mask / rk-bit t) 2 == 1

  rk-flood : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-flood (s) (p) (mask) (done) =
    let t = rk-next-open mask done 0
    in if t < 0 then mask
    else rk-flood s p (rk-expand s p t mask 0) (done + rk-bit t)

  rk-next-open : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-next-open (mask) (done) (t) =
    if t >= rk-territories then (-1)
    else if rk-has mask t & rk-has done t == False then t
    else rk-next-open mask done (t + 1)

  rk-expand : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-expand (s) (p) (t) (mask) (u) =
    if u >= rk-territories then mask
    else if rk-has mask u then rk-expand s p t mask (u + 1)
    else if rk-owner s u == p & rk-adjacent t u then rk-expand s p t (mask + rk-bit u) (u + 1)
    else rk-expand s p t mask (u + 1)

Section: What Each Player May Do

  rk-live : RiskState, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-live (s) (p) =
    if rk-over s then False
    else if p < 0 then False
    else if p >= rk-players s then False
    else True

  rk-terr-ok : Integer -> Boolean
  rk-terr-ok (t) = if t < 0 then False else t < rk-territories

  rk-legal : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-legal (s) (p) (kind) (arg) =
    if rk-live s p == False then False
    else if p /= rk-cur s then False
    else let ph = rk-phase s
    in if kind == 0 then rk-can-place s p ph arg
    else if kind == 1 then (if ph == 1 then rk-can-trade-cards s p arg else if ph == 5 then (if rk-hand s p >= 5 then rk-can-trade-cards s p arg else False) else False)
    else if kind == 2 then (if ph == 2 then rk-can-attack s p arg else False)
    else if kind == 3 then ph == 2
    else if kind == 4 then (if ph == 3 then (arg >= rk-get s rk-f-mmin) & (arg <= rk-armies s (rk-get s rk-f-mfrom) - 1) else False)
    else if kind == 5 then (if ph == 4 then rk-can-fortify s p arg else False)
    else if kind == 6 then ph == 4
    else False

  rk-can-place : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-can-place (s) (p) (ph) (t) =
    if rk-terr-ok t == False then False
    else if rk-owner s t /= p then False
    else if ph == 0 then rk-get s (rk-f-setup + p) > 0
    else if ph == 1 | ph == 5 then (if rk-get s rk-f-place <= 0 then False else rk-hand s p < 5)
    else False

  rk-can-attack : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-can-attack (s) (p) (packed) =
    let from = rk-unpack-a packed
    in let dest = rk-unpack-b packed
    in let dice = rk-unpack-c packed
    in if rk-terr-ok from == False | rk-terr-ok dest == False then False
    else if rk-owner s from /= p then False
    else if rk-owner s dest == p then False
    else if rk-adjacent from dest == False then False
    else if dice < 1 | dice > 3 then False
    else dice <= rk-armies s from - 1

  rk-can-fortify : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-can-fortify (s) (p) (packed) =
    let from = rk-unpack-a packed
    in let dest = rk-unpack-b packed
    in let n = rk-unpack-c packed
    in if rk-terr-ok from == False | rk-terr-ok dest == False then False
    else if from == dest then False
    else if rk-owner s from /= p | rk-owner s dest /= p then False
    else if n < 1 | n > rk-armies s from - 1 then False
    else rk-connected s p from dest

Section: Acting

  rk-act : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-act (s) (p) (kind) (arg) (seed) =
    if rk-legal s p kind arg then rk-act-in (rk-copy s) p kind arg seed else s

 The unchecked form writes into the state it is given.

  rk-act-in : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-act-in (s) (p) (kind) (arg) (seed) =
    if kind == 0 then rk-place s p arg
    else if kind == 1 then rk-trade s p arg
    else if kind == 2 then rk-attack s p arg seed
    else if kind == 3 then rk-put s rk-f-phase 4
    else if kind == 4 then rk-move-in s arg
    else if kind == 5 then rk-fortify s arg
    else if kind == 6 then rk-end-turn s
    else s

  rk-place : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-place (s) (p) (t) =
    let s2 = rk-set-armies s t (rk-armies s t + 1)
    in if rk-phase s2 == 0 then rk-setup-next (rk-put s2 (rk-f-setup + p) (rk-get s2 (rk-f-setup + p) - 1)) p
    else let left = rk-get s2 rk-f-place - 1
    in let s3 = rk-put s2 rk-f-place left
    in if left > 0 then s3
    else rk-put s3 rk-f-phase 2

  rk-setup-next : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-setup-next (s) (p) = rk-setup-next-loop s p 1

  rk-setup-next-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-setup-next-loop (s) (p) (k) =
    if k > rk-players s then rk-begin-turn (rk-put s rk-f-cur 0)
    else let q = rng-mod (p + k) (rk-players s)
    in if rk-get s (rk-f-setup + q) > 0 then rk-put s rk-f-cur q
    else rk-setup-next-loop s p (k + 1)

  rk-begin-turn : RiskState -> RiskState
  rk-begin-turn (s) =
    let p = rk-cur s
    in let s2 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s rk-f-conquered 0) rk-f-bonus 0) rk-f-elim 0
    in rk-put (rk-put s2 rk-f-place (rk-reinforcements s2 p)) rk-f-phase 1

 A battle: the attacker's dice are the first `dice` of the seed's dice 1 to
 3, the defender's its dice 4 and 5, each side sorted high to low.

  rk-attack : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-attack (s) (p) (packed) (seed) =
    let from = rk-unpack-a packed
    in let dest = rk-unpack-b packed
    in let n = rk-unpack-c packed
    in let m = if rk-armies s dest >= 2 then 2 else 1
    in let a1 = rk-die seed 1
    in let a2 = if n >= 2 then rk-die seed 2 else 0
    in let a3 = if n >= 3 then rk-die seed 3 else 0
    in let d1 = rk-die seed 4
    in let d2 = if m >= 2 then rk-die seed 5 else 0
    in let s2 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s rk-f-dice a1) (rk-f-dice + 1) a2) (rk-f-dice + 2) a3) (rk-f-dice + 3) d1) (rk-f-dice + 4) d2
    in rk-battle s2 p from dest n (rk-high3 a1 a2 a3) (rk-mid3 a1 a2 a3) (rk-high2 d1 d2) (rk-low2 d1 d2) m

  rk-high3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-high3 (a) (b) (c) = if a >= b & a >= c then a else if b >= c then b else c

  rk-mid3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-mid3 (a) (b) (c) =
    if a >= b & a >= c then (if b >= c then b else c)
    else if b >= a & b >= c then (if a >= c then a else c)
    else if a >= b then a
    else b

  rk-high2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-high2 (a) (b) = if a >= b then a else b

  rk-low2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-low2 (a) (b) = if a >= b then b else a

  rk-battle : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-battle (s) (p) (from) (dest) (n) (ah) (am) (dh) (dl) (m) =
    let first-a = if ah > dh then 0 else 1
    in let pairs = if n >= 2 & m >= 2 then 2 else 1
    in let second-a = if pairs == 2 then (if am > dl then 0 else 1) else 0
    in let alost = first-a + second-a
    in let dlost = pairs - alost
    in let s2 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s rk-f-alost alost) rk-f-dlost dlost) rk-f-rolled n
    in let s3 = rk-set-armies (rk-set-armies s2 from (rk-armies s2 from - alost)) dest (rk-armies s2 dest - dlost)
    in if rk-armies s3 dest > 0 then s3
    else rk-conquer s3 p from dest n

  rk-conquer : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-conquer (s) (p) (from) (dest) (n) =
    let q = rk-owner s dest
    in let s2 = rk-put (rk-put s (rk-tslot dest 0) p) rk-f-conquered 1
    in let s3 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s2 rk-f-mfrom from) rk-f-mto dest) rk-f-mmin n
    in if rk-held s3 p == rk-territories then rk-finish (rk-set-armies (rk-set-armies s3 dest n) from (rk-armies s3 from - n)) p
    else if rk-held s3 q > 0 then rk-put s3 rk-f-phase 3
    else let s4 = rk-take-cards s3 q p 0
    in rk-put (rk-put s4 rk-f-elim (if rk-hand s4 p >= 6 then 1 else 0)) rk-f-phase 3

  rk-finish : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-finish (s) (p) =
    rk-put (rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s rk-f-over 1) rk-f-winner p) rk-f-phase 6) rk-f-place 0

  rk-move-in : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-move-in (s) (n) =
    let from = rk-get s rk-f-mfrom
    in let dest = rk-get s rk-f-mto
    in let s2 = rk-set-armies (rk-set-armies s from (rk-armies s from - n)) dest n
    in let s3 = rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s2 rk-f-mfrom (-1)) rk-f-mto (-1)) rk-f-mmin 0
    in if rk-get s3 rk-f-elim == 1 then rk-put (rk-put (rk-put s3 rk-f-elim 0) rk-f-place 0) rk-f-phase 5
    else rk-put s3 rk-f-phase 2

  rk-fortify : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  rk-fortify (s) (packed) =
    let from = rk-unpack-a packed
    in let dest = rk-unpack-b packed
    in let n = rk-unpack-c packed
    in rk-end-turn (rk-set-armies (rk-set-armies s from (rk-armies s from - n)) dest (rk-armies s dest + n))

  rk-end-turn : RiskState -> RiskState
  rk-end-turn (s) =
    let p = rk-cur s
    in let s2 = if rk-get s rk-f-conquered == 1 then rk-draw s p else s
    in let s3 = rk-put (rk-put s2 rk-f-cur (rk-next-live s2 p 1)) rk-f-turn (rk-get s2 rk-f-turn + 1)
    in rk-begin-turn s3

  rk-next-live : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-next-live (s) (p) (k) =
    if k > rk-players s then p
    else let q = rng-mod (p + k) (rk-players s)
    in if rk-alive s q then q
    else rk-next-live s p (k + 1)

Section: The Engine's Players

 A choice is one action packed as kind + 8 * player + 64 * argument, or -1
 when there is none. The engine's players set up on their weakest border
 territory, trade the first set they hold whenever they may, reinforce
 their strongest border territory, attack from the strongest odds while the
 attacker has at least two more armies than the defender, rolling all the
 dice they may, move everything in when the attacking territory has no
 enemy left beside it and half otherwise, and fortify the strongest
 interior territory onto the weakest border territory joined to it.

  rk-code : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-code (kind) (p) (arg) = kind + 8 * p + 64 * arg

  rk-code-kind : Integer -> Integer
  rk-code-kind (c) = rng-mod c 8

  rk-code-player : Integer -> Integer
  rk-code-player (c) = rng-mod (c / 8) 8

  rk-code-arg : Integer -> Integer
  rk-code-arg (c) = c / 64

  rk-border-terr : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-border-terr (s) (p) (t) = rk-enemy-near s p t 0

  rk-enemy-near : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  rk-enemy-near (s) (p) (t) (u) =
    if u >= rk-territories then False
    else if rk-adjacent t u & rk-owner s u /= p then True
    else rk-enemy-near s p t (u + 1)

 The border territory with the fewest (`want-most` False) or most armies,
 lowest number first; -1 when the player has no border.

  rk-pick-border : RiskState, Integer, Boolean, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-pick-border (s) (p) (want-most) (t) (best) =
    if t >= rk-territories then best
    else if rk-owner s t /= p then rk-pick-border s p want-most (t + 1) best
    else if rk-border-terr s p t == False then rk-pick-border s p want-most (t + 1) best
    else if best < 0 then rk-pick-border s p want-most (t + 1) t
    else if want-most & rk-armies s t > rk-armies s best then rk-pick-border s p want-most (t + 1) t
    else if want-most == False & rk-armies s t < rk-armies s best then rk-pick-border s p want-most (t + 1) t
    else rk-pick-border s p want-most (t + 1) best

  rk-first-owned : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-first-owned (s) (p) (t) =
    if t >= rk-territories then (-1)
    else if rk-owner s t == p then t
    else rk-first-owned s p (t + 1)

  rk-ai-place-target : RiskState, Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  rk-ai-place-target (s) (p) (want-most) =
    let b = rk-pick-border s p want-most 0 (-1)
    in if b >= 0 then b else rk-first-owned s p 0

  rk-first-set : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-first-set (s) (p) (a) (b) (c) =
    if a >= 42 then (-1)
    else if b >= 43 then rk-first-set s p (a + 1) (a + 2) (a + 3)
    else if c >= 44 then rk-first-set s p a (b + 1) (b + 2)
    else if rk-holder s a /= p then rk-first-set s p (a + 1) (a + 2) (a + 3)
    else if rk-holder s b /= p then rk-first-set s p a (b + 1) (b + 2)
    else if rk-can-trade-cards s p (rk-pack a b c) then rk-pack a b c
    else rk-first-set s p a b (c + 1)

 The best attack: most attacking armies less defending armies, over pairs
 with the attacker at least two ahead; -1 when there is none.

  rk-best-attack : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-best-attack (s) (p) (from) (dest) (best) (best-gap) =
    if from >= rk-territories then best
    else if dest >= rk-territories then rk-best-attack s p (from + 1) 0 best best-gap
    else if rk-owner s from /= p | rk-owner s dest == p | rk-adjacent from dest == False then rk-best-attack s p from (dest + 1) best best-gap
    else let gap = rk-armies s from - rk-armies s dest
    in if gap >= 2 & gap > best-gap then rk-best-attack s p from (dest + 1) (rk-pack from dest 0) gap
    else rk-best-attack s p from (dest + 1) best best-gap

  rk-ai-fortify : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-ai-fortify (s) (p) =
    let from = rk-strongest-interior s p 0 (-1)
    in if from < 0 then (-1)
    else let dest = rk-weakest-joined-border s p from 0 (-1)
    in if dest < 0 then (-1)
    else rk-pack from dest (rk-armies s from - 1)

  rk-strongest-interior : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-strongest-interior (s) (p) (t) (best) =
    if t >= rk-territories then best
    else if rk-owner s t /= p | rk-armies s t < 2 | rk-border-terr s p t then rk-strongest-interior s p (t + 1) best
    else if best < 0 then rk-strongest-interior s p (t + 1) t
    else if rk-armies s t > rk-armies s best then rk-strongest-interior s p (t + 1) t
    else rk-strongest-interior s p (t + 1) best

  rk-weakest-joined-border : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-weakest-joined-border (s) (p) (from) (t) (best) =
    if t >= rk-territories then best
    else if rk-owner s t /= p | rk-border-terr s p t == False then rk-weakest-joined-border s p from (t + 1) best
    else if best >= 0 & rk-armies s t >= rk-armies s best then rk-weakest-joined-border s p from (t + 1) best
    else if rk-connected s p from t then rk-weakest-joined-border s p from (t + 1) t
    else rk-weakest-joined-border s p from (t + 1) best

  rk-ai : RiskState -> Integer
  rk-ai (s) =
    let p = rk-cur s
    in let ph = rk-phase s
    in if rk-over s then (-1)
    else if ph == 0 then rk-code 0 p (rk-ai-place-target s p False)
    else if ph == 1 | ph == 5 then rk-ai-reinforce s p ph
    else if ph == 2 then rk-ai-attack s p
    else if ph == 3 then rk-code 4 p (rk-ai-move-in s)
    else if ph == 4 then rk-ai-end s p (rk-ai-fortify s p)
    else (-1)

  rk-ai-end : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-ai-end (s) (p) (f) = if f >= 0 then rk-code 5 p f else rk-code 6 p 0

  rk-ai-reinforce : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rk-ai-reinforce (s) (p) (ph) =
    let set = rk-first-set s p 0 1 2
    in if set >= 0 & rk-legal s p 1 set then rk-code 1 p set
    else rk-code 0 p (rk-ai-place-target s p True)

  rk-ai-attack : RiskState, Integer -> Integer
  rk-ai-attack (s) (p) =
    let a = rk-best-attack s p 0 0 (-1) 0
    in if a < 0 then rk-code 3 p 0
    else let from = rk-unpack-a a
    in let most = rk-armies s from - 1
    in rk-code 2 p (rk-pack from (rk-unpack-b a) (if most > 3 then 3 else most))

  rk-ai-move-in : RiskState -> Integer
  rk-ai-move-in (s) =
    let from = rk-get s rk-f-mfrom
    in let most = rk-armies s from - 1
    in let least = rk-get s rk-f-mmin
    in if rk-border-terr s (rk-cur s) from == False then most
    else let half = most / 2
    in if half < least then least else half

Section: Stepping

 A step plays the engine's choices until the turn passes, the game ends,
 or the choice falls to the person when it did not start with them. The
 attack seed is the step's seed moved on for each choice.

  risk-step : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  risk-step (s) (seed) =
    if rk-over s then s
    else risk-step-in (rk-copy s) seed

  risk-step-in : RiskState, Integer -> RiskState
  risk-step-in (s) (seed) =
    let human = rk-get s rk-f-human
    in rk-step-loop s seed 0 (rk-get s rk-f-turn) (rk-cur s == human) (rk-phase s == 0)

  rk-step-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, Boolean -> RiskState
  rk-step-loop (s) (seed) (n) (turn) (theirs) (setup) =
    if rk-over s then s
    else if n >= 2000 then s
    else if (n > 0) & (setup == False) & (rk-get s rk-f-turn /= turn) then s
    else if (n > 0) & setup & (rk-phase s /= 0) then s
    else if (n > 0) & setup & (rk-cur s == rk-get s rk-f-human) then s
    else if (n > 0) & (theirs == False) & (rk-cur s == rk-get s rk-f-human) then s
    else let code = rk-ai s
    in if code < 0 then s
    else let kind = rk-code-kind code
    in let p = rk-code-player code
    in let arg = rk-code-arg code
    in let step-seed = seed + n * 7919
    in if rk-legal s p kind arg == False then s
    else rk-step-loop (rk-act-in s p kind arg step-seed) seed (n + 1) turn theirs setup

Section: Game Runner

  risk-turn-cap : Integer
  risk-turn-cap = 400

  run-risk-game : Integer, Integer -> RiskResult
  run-risk-game (seed) (num-players) =
    risk-loop (risk-init seed num-players) seed 0

  risk-loop : RiskState, Integer, Integer -> RiskResult
  risk-loop (s) (seed) (n) =
    if rk-over s then risk-make-result s
    else if rk-get s rk-f-turn >= risk-turn-cap then risk-make-result s
    else if n > 20000 then risk-make-result s
    else risk-loop (risk-step-in s (seed * 7919 + n * 104729)) seed (n + 1)

  risk-make-result : RiskState -> RiskResult
  risk-make-result (s) =
    RiskResult { winner = rk-get s rk-f-winner, turns = rk-get s rk-f-turn, territories = risk-collect-owners s 0 [] }

  risk-collect-owners : RiskState, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  risk-collect-owners (s) (t) (acc) =
    if t >= rk-territories then acc
    else risk-collect-owners s (t + 1) (list-push acc (rk-owner s t))

Section: Formatting

  format-risk-result : RiskResult -> Text
  format-risk-result (r) =
    let w = if r.winner < 0 then "None" else "P" & show (r.winner + 1)
    in "Risk (42 territories, " & show r.turns & " turns): winner=" & w

Page 1
